{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>The steadfast loves.</b> Then the discerning of Israel will give thanks for the abundance of steadfast loves that HaShem did for Israel when they went out from Egypt, also in exile, and that He saved them and restored them to their land." "And the meaning of <b>the praises of YHWH</b> — for mentioning HaShem's steadfast loves, this is His praise:" "<b>And great goodness.</b> An attribute of the Name, that He is great in goodness:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 63, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:00:45.461614662Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}